	(text_box "I2C at 400 kHz, 3.3 V, 2.2k pull-ups; on it: U3\n(LP5036, 0x30), the tree's LP5036 (0x31, through\nthe socket), U15 (LSM6DS3TR-C, 0x6A: taps and\ntilt), U16 (LTR-303, 0x29: the owls wake at\ndusk), U17 (TMAG5273A2, 0x35: times the\npendulum's kicks). Interrupts the firmware does\nnot use stay open." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 212.0900 403.8600 0) (size 44.4500 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d9bd4600-0e1c-b5c4-8b6c-b86b14f04aa5"))
	(text_box "U3, LP5036: 36 current sinks, 12-bit PWM at 29 kHz (no\nflicker a camera or an eye can see), in 12 banks of 3\nthat share a brightness. R3K3 on IREF sets the most any\noutput can sink: 105 x 0.7 V / 3.3k = 22 mA, under every\nLED's 30 mA, whatever the firmware asks. The LEDs'\nanodes are on 4.8 V; the names on the wires are\ngen/leds.py's, which the firmware's light show uses." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 17.7800 431.8000 0) (size 52.0700 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a9725c45-b1aa-330a-d55e-d9754356b028"))
